    "created_at": "2022-10-29T02:05:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-30T02:00:29Z",
    "body": "Could anyone be able to provide the current status of this proposal?\r\n\r\nI just ran into an issue related to this because I didn't realize the `referrer-policy` also controlled whether or not the `origin` header was set to a non-null value (at least in Firefox).  I have `no-referrer` set by default, but this makes it impossible to use the `origin` header for anything useful, since simple form posts always show null.  Instead of setting the `referrer-policy` at a page level, it'd be great to simply enable a more lax policy just for the specific forms.\r\n\r\nFrom https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#origin-header:\r\n\r\n> If request’s [mode](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-mode) is not \"cors\", then switch on request’s [referrer policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-referrer-policy):\r\n> If \"no-referrer\" ...\r\n> Set serializedOrigin to `null`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
